an impure entry is refused by Schedule.apply, naming the entry and the hidden write, before any op runs: true
schedule_legality refuses it too, naming the entry and the hidden write, with no verdict and no op dispatched: true
strict: the entry refusal is fatal, untyped (Invalid_argument, no cause): true
permissive: it is contained as Unclassified, never as Illegal_schedule, with no op dispatched: true
the empty schedule is the identity on the impure entry, dispatching nothing: true
op_legality admits an in-place unroll on the impure entry: true
the autotuner menu offers that unroll: true
applying the offered unroll refuses the hidden write before dispatch: true
the coalesce probe names the accumulator's unpaired index on both placements of the write: true
the statement-level twin reaches its ops and is refused at the Retype, naming the tile's lifetime: true
a pure entry holding a pure scope body runs every op: true
and schedule_legality dispatches every op of it too: true
judging none of them illegal: true
the unscheduled cells are distinct and moved off their seeds, so a swapped or dropped store-back would show: true
and computes the unscheduled program's values: true
a pure entry with a Grid loop inside a scope body is admitted, and its Retype to Serial repairs it: true
schedule_entry_scope_purity: done
